WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:34.000


2
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.041
<b>Arjuna continues to express his thoughts here.</b>

3
00:00:37.041 --> 00:00:38.500
<b>He says</b>

4
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.250
<b>that rather than killing his noble teachers,</b>
<b>it would be better for him</b>

5
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.458
<b> to live a life begging for alms. </b>

6
00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:47.833
<b>They are our gurus,</b>

7
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:53.791
<b>and even if killing them brings kingdom,</b>
<b>prosperity, or material comforts,</b>

8
00:00:53.791 --> 00:00:57.625
<b>won't that happiness be stained with their blood?</b>

9
00:00:57.625 --> 00:01:00.541
<b>Such happiness can't really be happiness at all.</b>

10
00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:05.500


11
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.916
<b>Arjuna thinks,</b>

12
00:01:06.916 --> 00:01:13.666
<b>if I commit the sin of killing my elders</b>
<b>in this war, I'll suffer forever.</b>

13
00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:18.083
<b>It's better to go into exile again.</b>

14
00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:23.541
<b>After all, I've already spent 13 years of my life</b>
<b>in the forest, so once more won't hurt.</b>

15
00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:29.458
<b>At least I won't bear the stigma of killing</b>
<b>my godlike teachers and elders.</b>

16
00:01:29.458 --> 00:01:31.083
<b>Arjuna is a warrior;</b>

17
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:35.500
<b>he knows that the warrior's duty</b>
<b>is valor, not begging.</b>

18
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.500
<b>But right now,</b>

19
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:40.875
<b>he considers begging better</b>
<b>than his warrior duty.</b>

20
00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:43.000
<b>Images are rising in his mind</b>

21
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:52.791
<b>as if any happiness, wealth, or object gained</b>
<b>from this war will be splattered with red blood.</b>

22
00:01:52.791 --> 00:01:54.875
<b>And this blood won't be of strangers,</b>

23
00:01:54.875 --> 00:01:56.416
<b>but of his grandfather,</b>

24
00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:59.541
<b>his teacher Drona, his own loved ones.</b>

25
00:01:59.541 --> 00:02:03.375
<b>This imagery is creating disgust in his mind.</b>

26
00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:07.333
<b>He's breaking, shattering inside.</b>

27
00:02:07.333 --> 00:02:10.083
<b>On one hand, he talks about begging,</b>

28
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:15.458
<b>and on the other, his mind pictures wealth</b>
<b>and happiness stained with blood.</b>

29
00:02:15.458 --> 00:02:22.166
<b>Such contradictions, such opposing thoughts,</b>
<b>are signs that he's now confused,</b>

30
00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:26.000
<b>caught in a whirlwind of uncertainty.</b>

31
00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:30.791


32
00:02:30.791 --> 00:02:34.666
<b>No matter how great a warrior</b>
<b>Arjuna has become,</b>

33
00:02:34.666 --> 00:02:40.583
<b>he hasn't forgotten his gratitude towards</b>
<b>his grandfather and his teacher Drona.</b>

34
00:02:40.583 --> 00:02:43.750
<b>They taught him in childhood,</b>

35
00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:48.500
<b>gave him affection, made him worthy</b>
<b>of wielding weapons.</b>

36
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:53.875
<b>Even though they stand with his enemy</b>
<b>Duryodhana today,</b>

37
00:02:53.875 --> 00:02:58.708
<b>Arjuna doesn't want to forget that</b>

38
00:02:58.708 --> 00:03:05.041
<b>who he is today is largely</b>
<b>due to their contribution.</b>

39
00:03:05.041 --> 00:03:11.875
<b>This contribution can't be denied just because</b>
<b>they now support the enemy.</b>

40
00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:13.000
<b>Yes,</b>

41
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:18.333
<b>he'll have to fight this war</b>
<b>for dharma eventually, </b>

42
00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:20.041
<b>but</b>

43
00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:24.541
<b>he'll never forget this feeling of gratitude.</b>

44
00:03:24.541 --> 00:03:29.416
<b>This sense of gratitude is worth learning.</b>

45
00:03:29.416 --> 00:03:35.708
<b>It's always worth remembering others' positive</b>
<b>contributions to our lives.</b>

46
00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:38.666
<b>When we do this,</b>

47
00:03:38.666 --> 00:03:42.083
<b>we see the good in all of them.</b>

48
00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:42.750
<b>And</b>

49
00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:48.875
<b>seeing good in others is a</b>
<b>crucial lesson for personal life.</b>

50
00:03:48.875 --> 00:03:50.666
<b>When we believe that</b>

51
00:03:50.666 --> 00:03:54.625
<b>people are generally good,</b>

52
00:03:54.625 --> 00:04:01.375
<b>we become more capable of</b>
<b>understanding their perspectives.</b>

53
00:04:01.375 --> 00:04:05.875
<b>We start to realize that</b>
<b>people aren't good or bad,</b>

54
00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:08.166
<b>just different.</b>

55
00:04:08.166 --> 00:04:09.375
<b>Different people, </b>

56
00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:10.791
<b>different viewpoints.</b>

57
00:04:10.791 --> 00:04:14.833
<b>And it's merely circumstances</b>

58
00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:22.916
<b>that put some in your support</b>
<b>and others against you.</b>

59
00:04:22.916 --> 00:04:25.958
<b>And this is the right mindset.</b>

60
00:04:25.958 --> 00:04:30.375
<b>It removes bitterness towards</b>
<b>others from your mind,</b>

61
00:04:30.375 --> 00:04:35.250
<b>which is essential for a pleasant personal life.</b>

62
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:39.833


63
00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:42.208
<b>Arjuna knows</b>

64
00:04:42.208 --> 00:04:46.083
<b>his enemy Duryodhana is unrighteous.</b>

65
00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:47.875
<b>He believes</b>

66
00:04:47.875 --> 00:04:55.583
<b>those supporting Duryodhanahave become party</b>
<b>to unrighteousness merely by association. </b>

67
00:04:55.583 --> 00:04:56.791
<b>Yet,</b>

68
00:04:56.791 --> 00:05:01.416
<b>at this moment, contrary to</b>
<b>their unrighteous conduct,</b>

69
00:05:01.416 --> 00:05:06.625
<b>he's looking for what makes them great.</b>

70
00:05:06.625 --> 00:05:08.416
<b>Arjuna thinks,</b>

71
00:05:08.416 --> 00:05:10.000
<b>why kill them?</b>

72
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.250
<b>These people are good.</b>

73
00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:19.125
<b>When you meet people in family or society,</b>

74
00:05:19.125 --> 00:05:22.541
<b>what do you see first?</b>

75
00:05:22.541 --> 00:05:24.333
<b>Their goodness</b>

76
00:05:24.333 --> 00:05:28.833
<b>or their flaws?</b>

77
00:05:28.833 --> 00:05:34.333
<b>Seeing people's good qualities adds</b>
<b>a sweetness to social relationships. </b>

78
00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:37.708
<b>Because when you see their good qualities,</b>

79
00:05:37.708 --> 00:05:40.916
<b>your behavior becomes gentle.</b>

80
00:05:40.916 --> 00:05:47.333
<b>And everyone likes someone</b>
<b>with gentle behavior.</b>

81
00:05:47.333 --> 00:05:49.708
<b>Think about it yourself.</b>

82
00:05:49.708 --> 00:05:54.416
<b>We remember those who speak sweetly to us,</b>

83
00:05:54.416 --> 00:05:58.916
<b>who make us feel good about ourselves.</b>

84
00:05:58.916 --> 00:06:02.500
<b>They can do this</b>

85
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.458
<b>because</b>

86
00:06:03.458 --> 00:06:08.875
<b>they see a good person in us.</b>

87
00:06:08.875 --> 00:06:12.000
<b>So now the question arises,</b>

88
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.833
<b>if everyone is good, </b>

89
00:06:14.833 --> 00:06:18.708
<b>should we befriend everyone?</b>

90
00:06:18.708 --> 00:06:22.958
<b>There are also people who wish us harm,</b>

91
00:06:22.958 --> 00:06:25.416
<b>what about them?</b>

92
00:06:25.416 --> 00:06:31.833
<b>It's necessary to stay away from</b>
<b>those who wish us harm.</b>

93
00:06:31.833 --> 00:06:35.166
<b>You're doing this for your own safety.</b>

94
00:06:35.166 --> 00:06:35.958
<b>But</b>

95
00:06:35.958 --> 00:06:41.791
<b>even those people are just bound</b>
<b>by their own perspective.</b>

96
00:06:41.791 --> 00:06:46.666
<b>Staying away from them</b>
<b>doesn't mean hating them.</b>

97
00:06:46.666 --> 00:06:47.458
<b>Because</b>

98
00:06:47.458 --> 00:06:50.625
<b> hate only makes you bitter.</b>

99
00:06:50.625 --> 00:06:53.791
<b>What use is that in life?</b>

100
00:06:53.791 --> 00:06:55.875
<b>See the good in people,</b>

101
00:06:55.875 --> 00:06:56.458
<b>and</b>

102
00:06:56.458 --> 00:06:58.625
<b>if you see any bad,</b>

103
00:06:58.625 --> 00:07:02.666
<b>just steer clear of that badness.</b>

104
00:07:03.166 --> 00:07:07.291


105
00:07:07.291 --> 00:07:10.583
<b>Arjuna's thoughts are stretching far.</b>

106
00:07:10.583 --> 00:07:19.083
<b>He's even assessing that after the war,</b>
<b>his mind might never find peace.</b>

107
00:07:19.083 --> 00:07:26.250
<b>In that case, he thinks exile or</b>
<b>begging is better than ruling a kingdom.</b>

108
00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:31.250
<b>It's necessary to evaluate the</b>
<b>consequences of any action.</b>

109
00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.333
<b>The bigger the task,</b>

110
00:07:33.333 --> 00:07:35.791
<b>the deeper this thought should be</b>

111
00:07:35.791 --> 00:07:42.791
<b>about how it will affect us</b>
<b>and others in the future.</b>

112
00:07:42.791 --> 00:07:50.041
<b>Far-sighted thinking is a major measure of</b>
<b>success in professional life.</b>

113
00:07:50.041 --> 00:07:53.000
<b>The selection of a head for</b>
<b>any large organization,</b>

114
00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:57.500
<b>or senior officers, is made by considering </b>

115
00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:00.250
<b>how far their thinking goes.</b>

116
00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:05.500
<b>Can they see future opportunities and</b>
<b>take advantage of them?</b>

117
00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:13.291
<b>Can they protect their colleagues and</b>
<b>the organization from future calamities?</b>

118
00:08:13.291 --> 00:08:18.666
<b>Don't just think about immediate gains or losses.</b>

119
00:08:18.666 --> 00:08:20.666
<b>Think long-term.</b>

120
00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:23.125
<b>When you do this,</b>

121
00:08:23.125 --> 00:08:26.875
<b>your approach to work will change,</b>

122
00:08:26.875 --> 00:08:31.458
<b>which is essential for success in professional life.</b>

